# STRICT BEHAVIOR RULES
1. THINK BEFORE ACTING: Always analyze the entire component structure and CSS hierarchy before editing any code.
2. NO PARTIAL CODE: Never replace files with placeholder code or truncated logic. Always provide fully functional code.
3. CSS ANIMATIONS PREFERENCE: Prefer modern CSS View Timeline and native Sticky positioning over heavy/buggy JS scroll hooks.
4. PRESERVE GLASSMORPHISM: Never change dark translucent backgrounds (bg-neutral-900/50, backdrop-blur) to solid black.
5. EXPLAIN PLAN BRIEFLY: Keep chat responses extremely concise. Focus 90% of your tokens on code accuracy.